1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:01,390
You can't tickle yourself.

2
00:00:01,670 --> 00:00:03,230
Your brain sees it coming.

3
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:06,500
Every time you move, it predicts what the touch will feel like,

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,110
and turns the feeling down.

5
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:11,990
In one experiment, people tickled their own hand through a robot.

6
00:00:12,290 --> 00:00:13,520
When it copied them instantly,

7
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:14,910
it barely tickled.

8
00:00:15,210 --> 00:00:17,120
Add a delay of a fraction of a second,

9
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:18,570
and the tickle came back.

10
00:00:18,870 --> 00:00:20,850
The same trick starts poke wars.

11
00:00:21,210 --> 00:00:24,540
In another study, two people took turns pressing each other's finger,

12
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:26,080
trying to match what they felt.

13
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:28,520
Their own press always felt softer,

14
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:30,110
so every turn got harder.

15
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:32,150
So go ahead, try it right now.

16
00:00:32,270 --> 00:00:33,270
It won't work, because
